{"assets":["/statement-assets/dfd71bdf2225df5b1895037b8f5a3014a923c5e4b4ba4b7b54860fc4c7e573c8.png","/statement-assets/cd5e99ec1f07908bcbc1596f0a5cd4d5b2935a332e75d1fef5383f54c53ef01f.png","/statement-assets/14ca2f946d09e6056dff206d83227be67c160aca19ee08c40725a15b82ed3531.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1172","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Nauuo and Portals"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Nauuo is a girl who loves playing games related to portals."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"One day she was playing a game as follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In an $$$n\\times n$$$ grid, the rows are numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ from top to bottom, the columns are numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ from left to right. We denote a cell on the intersection of the $$$r$$$-th row and $$$c$$$-th column as $$$(r,c)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A portal is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a pair of"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" doors. You can travel from one of them to another without changing your direction. More formally, if you "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"walk into"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" a cell with a door, you will teleport to the cell with the other door of the same portal and then "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"walk into"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"next cell"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" facing the original direction. There "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"can not"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" be more than one doors in a single cell."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"next cell"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" is the nearest cell in the direction you are facing. For example, if you are facing bottom, the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"next cell"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$(2,5)$$$ is $$$(3,5)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If you "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"walk into"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" a cell without a door, you must "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"walk into"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"next cell"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" after that without changing the direction. If the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"next cell"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" does not exist, you must exit the grid."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have to set some (possibly zero) portals in the grid, so that if you "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"walk into"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$(i,1)$$$ facing right, you will eventually exit the grid from $$$(r_i,n)$$$, if you "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"walk into"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$(1, i)$$$ facing bottom, you will exit the grid from $$$(n,c_i)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that both $$$r_{1..n}$$$ and $$$c_{1..n}$$$ are "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"permutations"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$n$$$ elements. A permutation of $$$n$$$ elements is a sequence of numbers $$$p_1,p_2,\\ldots,p_n$$$ in which every integer from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ appears exactly once."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"She got confused while playing the game, can you help her to find a solution?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1\\le n\\le 1000$$$) — the side length of the grid."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$r_1,r_2,\\ldots,r_n$$$ ($$$1\\le r_i\\le n$$$) — if you walk into $$$(i,1)$$$ facing right, you should exit the grid from $$$(r_i,n)$$$. It is guaranteed that $$$r_{1..n}$$$ is a permutation of $$$n$$$ elements."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$c_1,c_2,\\ldots,c_n$$$ ($$$1\\le c_i\\le n$$$) — if you walk into $$$(1,i)$$$ facing bottom, you should exit the grid from $$$(n,c_i)$$$. It is guaranteed that $$$c_{1..n}$$$ is a permutation of $$$n$$$ elements."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If it is impossible to satisfy the rule, print the only number $$$-1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Otherwise the first line should contain a single integer $$$m$$$ ($$$0\\le m\\le\\frac{n^2}2$$$) — the number of portals you set."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the following $$$m$$$ lines, each line should contain four integers $$$x_1,y_1,x_2,y_2$$$, represents that you set a portal consisting of two doors in $$$(x_1,y_1)$$$ and $$$(x_2,y_2)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are multiple answers, print any. You do "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"not"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" have to minimize $$$m$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n1 3 2\n3 1 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n1 1 1 3\n2 2 3 1"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n3 1 5 4 2\n4 2 1 3 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n1 1 3 4\n2 2 3 2\n2 3 5 1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example 1"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The cells with the same letter are a portal. You can set portals in this way:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/dfd71bdf2225df5b1895037b8f5a3014a923c5e4b4ba4b7b54860fc4c7e573c8.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It satisfies the rule, because:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/cd5e99ec1f07908bcbc1596f0a5cd4d5b2935a332e75d1fef5383f54c53ef01f.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example 2"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can set portals in this way:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/14ca2f946d09e6056dff206d83227be67c160aca19ee08c40725a15b82ed3531.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1172D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1172/problem/D"}